From 2d5fafb1b6f435f4b36d96caa6734537fff818ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:30:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Timeline day columns fill the full available width

Columns were fixed at 220px each, leaving a large dead gray area to
the right whenever an event had fewer tags/columns than fit the
viewport. Columns now flex to fill available width (flex-grow) while
keeping a 220px minimum (flex-shrink: 0 + minWidth) so the horizontal
scroll/drag-to-create behavior for many columns is unaffected.

Shift-block lane positioning (for overlapping shifts sharing a column)
switched from fixed-pixel widths derived from the old constant column
width to percentage-based widths, since column width is now dynamic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qm1ZJgsnaADwCEstGj8Dvj
